  "content": {
    "title": "'Tatted Like a Chipotle Bag' BOGO will last 1 hour on Friday the 13th",
    "text": "March 13, 2026, 6:01 a.m. ETChipotle is offering a buy-one-get-one deal on Friday, March 13, from 3 to 4 p.m.To receive the offer, customers must show a tattoo to the restaurant staff.The promotion accepts permanent, temporary or even drawn-on tattoos.Being tatted like a Chipotle bag – don't worry, not literally or even figuratively − will pay off March 13.On Friday the 13th, a date that's a big deal for tattoo artists and enthusiasts, the burritos-and-bowls chain will offer a one-hour buy-one-get-one deal between 3 and 4 p.m. You just have to show your tattoos − one, many, permanent, temporary, or drawn-on – to restaurant staff.Chipotle did this before. On June 13, 2025, the chain said, its \"Tatted Like a Chipotle Bag\" BOGO brought in its highest-ever sales for the non-peak hour.The restaurant company seems pretty lenient on what counts as a tattoo, even bringing in tattooed hip-hop artist Swae Lee to help design a temporary tattoo flash sheet for the occasion that will be given out in his hometown of Miami.For the rest of us, Chipotle will even accept \"any creative iteration invoking tattoos\" and has left it to \"the sole discretion of restaurant staff\" to decide what that means.The offer is good at participating Chipotle locations among its 52 in central Ohio.Follow Dispatch dining reporter Bob Vitale on Instagram at @dispatchdining. You can reach him directly at rvitale@dispatch.com.",
    "word_count": 229,
    "extraction_method": "readability"
  },
